# In what year did half of the world's people first use the internet?
subtitle: "Guess the year half of humanity first got online, then see the hundred-person world: who is still offline, and where."
tags: ["computing","data","geography"]
format: quiz
thumb: "band \"Half the world online. When?\" stamp \"Which year?\""

## In what year did half of the world's people first use the internet?
sources:
    - id: owid_net
      title: Share of the population using the Internet
      authors: Our World in Data, from the International Telecommunication Union (ITU) via the World Bank
      year: 2026
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/share-of-individuals-using-the-internet
      finding: 'world: 15.6 % in 2005, 22.8 % in 2008, 49.4 % in 2018, 53.9 % in 2019, 73.6 % in 2025; high-income countries 94 % and low-income countries 23 % in 2025'

    scale yr cites ["owid_net"] x 70 y 420 width 860 min 1990 max 2025 value 2019 ticks 7 tick_format numerals era none markers [{"value":2005,"label":"2005: 1 in 6"}] hidden true
    population crowd cites ["owid_net"] fit.h 390 fit.w 800 fit.x 100 fit.y 200 colors.offline #b5482e colors.online #2f6b8f count 100 states.offline 26 states.online 74 order rows labels.offline offline labels.online online hidden true
    population rich cites ["owid_net"] fit.h 300 fit.w 420 fit.x 40 fit.y 250 colors.offline #b5482e colors.online #2f6b8f count 100 states.offline 6 states.online 94 order rows labels.offline offline labels.online online hidden true
    text rich_t "Rich countries: 94" #2f6b8f cites ["owid_net"] x 250 y 605 font_size 46 hidden true
    population poor cites ["owid_net"] fit.h 300 fit.w 420 fit.x 540 fit.y 250 colors.offline #b5482e colors.online #2f6b8f count 100 states.offline 77 states.online 23 order rows labels.offline offline labels.online online hidden true
    text poor_t "Poorest: 23" #b5482e cites ["owid_net"] x 750 y 605 font_size 46 hidden true
    text echo "= the world in 2008" #b5482e cites ["owid_net"] x 750 y 205 font_size 44 hidden true

    card title "When did half the world get online?"

In what year did half of the world's people first use the internet?
    draw yr

    ask "Click on the line where you think it is." on yr store y default "2008" after keep
        right: Close. Half the world came online later than most people think.
        wrong: Not that year. See where the halfway point really falls.

Only in 2019. As late as 2005, it was about one person in six.
    draw yr_marker_1

    erase yr yr_answer yr_marker_1

And today? Picture the world as a hundred people. About seventy-four are online.
    draw crowd

Which leaves the second question: who are the other twenty-six? More than two billion people.
    highlight crowd_offline

    erase crowd

They are not spread evenly. In rich countries, ninety-four in a hundred are online.
    draw rich rich_t

In the poorest countries, twenty-three.
    draw poor poor_t

That is where the w (@draw echo@)hole world stood in 2008. The second half of the internet is still arriving.

And these seventy-seven are the people it's arriving for.
    highlight poor_offline

